From e760db0f2edb661648b113083cbd795bfbcd2241 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexanderNyr <131390634+AlexanderNyr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:09:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PERF P2: coherent success-only translation cache

P1-followup gprof: translate 79,798,615 calls and 22.10% sampled CPU in five boot runs. Add a 256-slot machine-wide TLB keyed by 4KiB VA subpage, CR3/CR0/CR4/EFER/AC/CPL/desc_sv/mode. Cache only successful walks over ordinary RAM-backed page-table entries with A20 open. Preserve every old fault walk and delivery. Invalidations: all guest/device-DMA RAM stores (global generation), CR0/CR3/CR4, LMSW, WRMSR EFER, no-fault INVLPG, machine reset and loader direct pre-execution table construction.

Same-patch test_tlb.c asserts warm hit and PTE 5MiB-to-6MiB remap; same-value control writes and INVLPG, exact nonpresent/NX/WP/U/S fault CR2/error/RIP, 2MiB/1GiB leaves, A20-off, dynamic MMIO root, SMP context keys. Single NC removes only RAM-store invalidation in a scratch mem.c: NEW_VALUE assertion fails, inner RC=134/script RC=1/make RC=2. Boot stats: 15,863,692 hits, 4,668 misses, 4,669 flushes; post-profile mem_read calls 313,666,250 to 78,188,375 across five runs. Two alternate pre/post triples kept all seven work counts identical; local wall ratios 1.15-1.35x, not an absolute gate.

Measured make test RC=0, make test-sanitize RC=0, make fuzz FUZZ_PROGRAMS=256 RC=0 (6,144 compared, 0 host crashes), make bench BENCH_REPS=3 RC=0. Four historical firmware/video stdout/log/PPM pairs byte-identical with no --stats. Frozen guest lanes SKIP without toolchain. See PERF_PLAN.md, CHANGELOG, ROADMAP, STATUS.
